/**
 * ADR-0124 section 16: the harder synthetic set v2 (phase 0, no model). A SEPARATE hash-frozen set; the v1 corpus and the
 * Drive-format variant are untouched. Generated by code from the fixed seed `quoky-adr-0124-ch1-v2-2026-11-05`, fictional
 * names only (v1's syllable tables), Korean / English / mixed.
 *
 * v1 was too easy to tell whether chunking should differ by data type: every question carried the needle's rare codename, no
 * paragraph passed the 1,200 code-point passage cap and no question named a section. v2 adds five difficulty features, tagged
 * per case so results can be stratified by feature:
 *
 *   1. paraphrase     the question identifies the needle by the topic it belongs to and the attribute asked about, in other
 *                     words (a synonym phrase, other particles), never by the needle's codename or its answer value.
 *   2. long-paragraph the needle sits inside ONE paragraph of 1,300-4,000 code points (no blank line), so the chunker's
 *                     sentence split and overlap path runs; lp-middle (needle in the middle third) or lp-cut (the needle's
 *                     sentence starts at the sentence boundary nearest the 800 code point passage target, clamped to what the
 *                     requested depth allows).
 *   3. section-name   (Drive doc and ADR file) the question names the section by its title ("in the Refund policy part (section 3)",
 *                     "3장 환불 정책 부분에서") and carries no topic; the needle sits in that section and no same-kind decoy
 *                     shares the section. A Drive doc is rendered as a plain-text AND a Markdown case with identical content.
 *   4. near-duplicate close decoys of the needle's own kind and template (other topic and codename, the answer value changed):
 *                     quoted earlier messages with `>` markers (mail, thread), repeated template paragraphs (Drive, Jira
 *                     comments, Slack replies, ADR file), look-alike sheet rows, near-identical code lines in a fenced block.
 *   5. dense          three times the same-kind decoys, plus decoys that reuse the question's attribute words and decoys that
 *                     name the target topic without the answer.
 *
 * GENERIC RULES WRITTEN BEFORE ANY RUN (not tuned on results): a paraphrase or section question must not contain the codename,
 * any answer value, or the needle's own topic phrase (the generator throws, so a degenerate case cannot exist); the needle text
 * occurs once in the prepared item. Template banks (topics, question and decoy templates) were written before any scorer ran.
 */
